    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.27). **Gunnar Henderson** is our premier play, benefiting from a massive 19% SP skill boost against Johnson; he is currently our most efficient option to stabilize our R/HR/RBI metrics. **Jackson Merrill** also enjoys an ideal matchup against Ritchie, with a 13% dynamic platoon advantage driving his elite score. **Andy Pages** (72.83) rounds out the top tier, utilizing his favorable placement in the two-hole against Rojas to provide excellent value. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.05) is batting against the capable Lambert, his consistent contact profile keeps him comfortably in the lineup as a utility lock.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Josh Jung** (53.10), who narrowly missed the cut behind the stability of **Drake Baldwin** (57.95) and **Nolan Schanuel** (55.75). While **Josh Jung** is historically solid, his park factors against Alcantara were slightly suppressed, leading us to favor the offensive environment surrounding **Coby Mayo** (54.99). We are keeping a close eye on **Dominic Smith** (47.00); despite his marginal score, his inclusion is necessitated by the current roster construction. **Nasim Nunez** (44.29) remains the primary threat to jump into the lineup if we decide to pivot toward a higher stolen base ceiling later in the day, though his matchup against the difficult Luzardo mandates caution. \n\nRegarding risks, we are monitoring the matchup for **Jacob Wilson** (61.49). Despite a tough assignment against Ray, **Jacob Wilson** maintains a strong score thanks to a favorable dynamic platoon advantage and a premium spot in the order. Conversely, we have benched **Curtis Mead** (39.56) entirely, as his sub-40 projection\u2014driven by the poor matchup against Luzardo\u2014falls below our threshold for maintaining game caps. We are proceeding with our current configuration, prioritizing the high-upside matchups for **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jackson Merrill** to maximize our daily scoring output.",
